UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p> The structure and program of offerings in the Fine Arts major make it the only one of its kind in Australia. Following a foundational first year of study in which you develop fundamental practical skills in tandem with a body of conceptual and theoretical knowledge, you then design your own focus in a variety of artistic fields. These focused areas of creative practice include (though are not limited to) drawing, painting, printmaking, sculpture, photography, art and biotechnologies, digital arts, generative AI arts, animation, film, environmental arts, social practice, and curatorial practice. <br/> <br/> Over the course of your second and third year of studio-based practice you will incrementally develop skills and expertise in one or more of these focus areas, with complementary studies in areas that align with your individual interests to support your creative work. Engaging with skills and processes across both established and emergent mediums, our cutting-edge creative units go beyond the studio into diverse settings such as science laboratories, regional and international communities, and landscapes undergoing rapid environmental change. Providing a comprehensive practical and theoretical foundation for creative exploration, the Fine Arts major at UWA empowers you with the opportunity to artistically articulate and debate the most challenging and difficult issues facing our world. </p>',
