    course_description = '<p>Landscape architects respond to challenges such as climate change and biodiversity loss by applying systems thinking and practice to develop long‑term, large‑scale solutions.<br/> <br/> The Landscape Architecture Studies let''s you to grow your creative, ecological and design skills while giving you the flexibility to combine your studies with another area of study that suit your interest.<br/> <br/> In this major you''ll develop ways of understanding landscapes and communities, learn how to design and plan for dynamic and resilient environments, and gain essential skills in critical thinking. You’ll graduate with strong theoretical and practical knowledge that enable you to produce creative landscape design outcomes. This major also provides a strong foundation for postgraduate study in landscape architecture or related fields.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = NULL,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University of Western Australia welcomes applications from international and domestic school-leavers. If you’re interested in studying one of these majors, find out the admission details below. </p> <!-- RichTextCourseCard.cshtml --> Admission requirements <p> For applicants with recent secondary education, information on admission criteria is available on our <a href="/study/how-to-apply/entry-requirements">entry requirements</a> page or on the <a href="https://handbooks.uwa.edu.au/">UWA Handbook</a> for course specific requirements and prerequisites.<br/> </p> Admission requirements <!-- RichTextCourseCard.cshtml --> Landscape Architecture Pathways for mature-age students <p> If you will be aged 20 years or older on 1 March (for Semester 1 entry) or 1 August (for Semester 2 entry) you qualify for our mature-age-entry pathways. </p> Landscape Architecture Pathways for mature-age students <!-- RichTextCourseCard.cshtml --> ADMISSION REQUIREMENT English competency <p>English is the language of instruction and assessment at UWA and you will need to meet the <a href="https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/how-to-apply/english-language-requirements">English language requirements</a> of the University to be eligible for a place.</p> <p>Minimum overall IELTS score of 6.5, with no band less than 6.0.</p> ADMISSION REQUIREMENT English competency',
    apply_form = 'https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/courses/landscape-architecture-studies',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '078213J';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>How does law shape our lives and the world around us? In the Law and Society major, you can engage with human rights, crime and justice, Indigenous legal systems, international law, and how the law shapes health and medicine, freedom of expression, social media and other aspects of society. You will explore the real-world impact of law and legal institutions on people’s lives and investigate the symbiotic relationship between legal change and social change. </p> <p>With its focus on the social dimensions of law, this major perfectly complements a wide range of studies including in politics, communications, psychology, criminology, gender studies, economics or anthropology. </p> <p>In the Law and Society major you will develop skills in research, critical thinking, problem-solving, and communication. These skills enable graduates to pursue varied careers in the private, non-profit and public sectors, including law-related policy and research roles. Graduates may work in law reform and justice agencies, the civil and criminal justice systems, government, education and academia, and law-relevant fields like politics, compliance and corporate social responsibility, regulation, management and human resources, media and communications, industrial relations, human rights, social services and legal support.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = NULL,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
